<title>FRANCE: MATIF financial futures volume rose in June.</title>
<headline>MATIF financial futures volume rose in June.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-07-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The volume of financial futures and options contracts traded on the French MATIF exchange in June rose 8.4 percent from the previous month and rose 25.9 percent compared to June 1997, Matif said in a statement on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Detailed figures for financial contracts were as follows:</p>
<p>			   Volume     Change    Change  Open positions</p>
<p>					 on month   on year  at end-month</p>
<p> All contracts	7.02 bln   +8.4 pct   +25.9 pct   952,130</p>
<p>  Financial futures 5.83 bln  +16.7 pct   +20.9 pct   530,684</p>
<p>Of which:</p>
<p>     -  French bond 3.64 bln  +24.9 pct   +22.9 pct   206,247</p>
<p>     -  PIBOR	 1.53 bln   +2.1 pct   +17.9 pct   251,080</p>
<p>     -  CAC-40	 617,720  +11.2 pct   +19.7 pct    67,904</p>
<p>     -  Ecu bond	43,170  +42.0 pct    -3.2 pct     5,041</p>
<p>     -  Bobl		 450    n/a	   n/a	     407</p>
<p>     -  LYS yield spds     0    n/a	   n/a		 5</p>
<p>  Financial options 1.20 bln  -19.6 pct   +57.7 pct   421,446</p>
<p>Of which:</p>
<p>     -  French bond  894,470  -10.1 pct   +58.3 pct   199,041</p>
<p>     -  PIBOR	  290,854  -40.2 pct   +57.8 pct   217,865</p>
<p>     -  Bobl	     9,300    n/a	   n/a	   3,000</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +331 4221 5542</p>
</text>
